    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d522">

                <pb facs="0567" n="469" xml:id="pg469"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/425: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-09-20T21:00:00+08:00">September 20, 1930—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 21—12:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>834. Department’s 312, September 8, 6 p.m.<anchor n="67" xml:id="d522-f1"/>
                    Legation has received final text of extraterritoriality proposals as handed in
                    by Lampson. There are certain changes in the June 4th draft in the preamble and
                    in articles 2, 9, 10 and 15. The protocol has been added. In case the British
                    Embassy has not supplied Department with text of these changes should they be
                    telegraphed?</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
